  "id": "COMPOUND:1727 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "Castanospermine is implicated in the regulation of Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Castanospermine acts as a target for multiple compounds, which in turn target the SDR family member 9. These compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate, (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, are all known to interact with the SDR family member 9. The shared target of these compounds points to a potential mechanism where Castanospermine may influence the activity of the SDR family member 9 through these intermediates. The evidence is consistent with a pathway where Castanospermine indirectly affects the SDR family member 9 via these compounds, highlighting a possible role in metabolic or enzymatic regulation. The integration of these pathways suggests a complex network of interactions that may be critical for the biological effects of Castanospermine.",
